# Patela local demo: optional keys for `npm run demo`.
# Copy to .env.demo (git-ignored) and fill in only what you want to switch on.
# With this file empty or absent, everything runs locally with no accounts:
# Hardhat chain 31337, MockZARP, Postgres in Docker (or PGlite), demo inbox instead of email.
# Values set in your shell override this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ports
# DEMO_WEB_PORT=3001
# DEMO_API_PORT=4000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Database
# Use your own Postgres instead of the Docker container / PGlite fallback.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:password@localhost:5432/patela
# Keep PGlite data between runs (default: fresh database each run, matching the fresh chain).
# DEMO_KEEP_DATA=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Google Maps (3D buyer map)
# Browser key with Maps JavaScript API + Map Tiles API enabled, restricted to http://localhost:3001/*.
# Without it the buyer dashboard shows its "map unavailable" fallback.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=
# Server key for POST /orders/:id/route (Routes API). Without it the route endpoint answers 502 "not configured".
# GOOGLE_MAPS_SERVER_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Google Speech (/voice/*)
# Path to a service-account JSON with Speech-to-Text and Text-to-Speech enabled.
# Without it /voice/transcribe and /voice/speak answer an error. No page calls them yet: the voice
# UI (with a browser Web Speech fallback) is still to be built.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=C:/path/to/service-account.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Google sign-in (optional)
# Email-code sign-in always works. These add "Continue with Google".
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Testnet instead of the local chain
# Set all four to skip the Hardhat node and use contracts you deployed with
#   cd contracts && npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.ts --network baseSepolia
# (needs BASE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL and DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY in the Hardhat keystore or env).
# Demo personas then stop signing (they only work on 31337): use MetaMask (buyer) and
# MetaMask Embedded Wallets (supplier, driver), which need NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3AUTH_CLIENT_ID.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=84532
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://sepolia.base.org
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ESCROW_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZARP_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# Backend RPC if it should differ from the browser's; confirmations before a tx counts.
# BASE_RPC_URL=
# CHAIN_CONFIRMATIONS=2
# Celo instead: NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=11142220 (Celo Sepolia, real Mento ZARm). The backend
# verifies Base chains and the local chain only, so Celo needs the feat/celo-* backend.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Real email (turns the demo inbox off)
# AWS Secrets Manager ARN holding the Gmail user + app password (see backend/README.md).
# SMTP_SECRET_ARN=arn:aws:secretsmanager:af-south-1:123456789012:secret:patela-smtp
# AWS_REGION=af-south-1
# AWS_PROFILE=default

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Deploying to AWS (not used by npm run demo)
# infra/backend-lambda.yaml and infra/amplify-hosting.yaml take these as stack parameters;
# see infra/README.md. Deploy only after approving the monthly cost.
# AWS_REGION=af-south-1
